{"title":"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain school, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as many boys as girls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as many girls as teachers. Using the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01c707400511c337caa1b9eafa910a6f051f1059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, g, t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> to represent the number of boys, girls, and teachers, respectively, then the total number of boys, girls, and teachers can be represented by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expression</a>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fee03f873a83fe0929e92ed7d5b669fcbd436ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }31b \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\frac{37b}{27} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 13g \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }\\frac{37g}{27} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{37t}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"439\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the given, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7565fb0560976b1f68e99250808510b45d4f7a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3g=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b79de138fef15596d5bf2c6588e2a9d4039efc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9t=g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578d5fde4bdc2d1450cd35cf17f07630679bc288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{g}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"33\" />. The sum of these, in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d448169c9a5bfd133b467ed972dbee81864f1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3g+g+\\frac{g}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"83\" height=\"33\" />, or, with a common <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Denominator\" title=\"Denominator\">denominator</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d54e6a3c221aee9cf22217af7e1580db215289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{37g}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"30\" height=\"37\" />. We can see that this isn't one of the choices. So we write it in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. We can see from the first <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362da45fcd55648ac961e6647587cd098d6badc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{b}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />, so substituting this into the expression yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7ef14988a87b17ffcc3867ad77bce218f373f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{37b}{27}, \\boxed{\\text{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME\" title=\"1984 AHSME\">1984 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1984 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Prob